  "text": "Science & Exploration Mars Express Investigating the Red Planet The mission Since beginning science operations in 2004, Mars Express has provided breathtaking views of Mars in three dimensions. It has provided the most complete map of the chemical composition of the atmosphere, studied Mars’s innermost moon Phobos in unprecedented detail, and traced the history of water across the globe, demonstrating that Mars once harboured environmental conditions that may have been suitable for life. Launch date: 2 June 2003 Arrival at Mars: December 2003 Status: In operation Targets: Mars's atmosphere, surface and subsurface; Mars's moons Phobos and Deimos 10 m imaging resolution 8 instruments 1120 kg launch mass 2 decades of operation Latest All Stories Videos Images Image Science & Exploration ESA’s Mars Express meets NASA’s Psyche 17/07/2026 2210 views 52 likes View Story Science & Exploration Metallic waves on ancient Mars 15/07/2026 3037 views 58 likes Read Story Science & Exploration Dozens of dust devils hidden in plain sight 17/06/2026 3327 views 48 likes Read Story Science & Exploration ExoMars rover targets vast bed of clay in search for life 04/06/2026 4252 views 57 likes Read Story Science & Exploration Waterworn chaos on Mars 13/05/2026 4507 views 100 likes Read Story Science & Exploration Ash creeps across Mars 15/04/2026 12979 views 93 likes Read Video 00:03:16 Science & Exploration Fly over Xanthe Terra with Mars Express 02/10/2025 9069 views 192 likes Play Video 00:04:30 Science & Exploration Fly around Ares Vallis on Mars 20/11/2024 9210 views 210 likes Play Video 00:03:29 Science & Exploration Fly across Nili Fossae with ESA’s Mars Express 29/05/2024 3705 views 55 likes Play Image Science & Exploration Sand dunes meet stacked ice at Mars’s north pole 28/02/2024 3606 views 39 likes View Image Science & Exploration Return to the labyrinth 24/01/2024 6179 views 67 likes View Video 00:03:44 Science & Exploration Fly across Mars’s ‘labyrinth of night’ with Mars Express 10/10/2023 14010 views 294 likes Play Image Science & Exploration 20 years and counting: Mars Express in numbers 02/06/2023 7278 views 115 likes View Image Science & Exploration Close-up of Valles Marineris from global Mars colour mosaic… 23/05/2023 7553 views 76 likes View Video 00:03:03 Science & Exploration Journey through Jezero 21/03/2023 11170 views 261 likes Play More items Image Science & Exploration Global Mars in colour 23/05/2023 24791 views 477 likes View Image Science & Exploration Ius and Tithonium Chasmata on Mars 20/07/2022 5726 views 83 likes View Image Science & Exploration Utopia Planitia on Mars 30/03/2022 6945 views 100 likes View Image Science & Exploration Perspective view along icy layered ridge 22/12/2022 2304 views 52 likes View Video Science & Exploration Fly over Xanthe Terra with Mars Express 02/10/2025 9069 views 192 likes Play Mars Express overview Focus on Science & Exploration Mars Express overview Open Focus on Science & Exploration Mars Express science highlights Open Focus on Science & Exploration Mars Express in-depth Open More About Mars Express Mars Express orbiter instruments The mission The spacecraft The launcher Frequently asked questions About Mars Geography of Mars Was there water on early Mars? Facts about Mars Europe reclaims a stake in Mars exploration Meet the team International collaboration Mission team Industry Multimedia Mars Express images Mars Express videos Mars Webcam Mars images mapped Follow us @science.esa.int ESA Space Science @esascience @ESAMarsWebcam European Space Agency FAQ Contacts Terms and conditions Privacy notice Careers at ESA Subscribe",
